From 6696c194cb7433300a7fdd7977411dfffe4dbac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:02:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] Use American spelling and state campaign retries
 precisely

Rename the manual's example unknown field to color and update its shown
error message. The manual and the architecture guide now say that only
complete, invalid and infeasible campaign records are cached, and that
work-limited, time-limited and canceled attempts stay in the journal
and are retried.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/architecture.md | 4 ++--
 docs/user-manual.md  | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 9360ef9..d095e03 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -152,8 +152,8 @@ and train dynamics are outside the supported input.
 
 The local campaign hashes the installed extension bytes plus each scenario, model,
 candidate and work settings to locate reusable records. SQLite stores completed, invalid
-and infeasible results, and keeps an append-only journal of attempts. Cancelled or
-time-limited attempts remain in the journal and can be retried. SQLite commits each chunk
+and infeasible results, and keeps an append-only journal of attempts. Work-limited,
+time-limited and canceled attempts remain only in the journal and are retried. SQLite commits each chunk
 atomically. A new extension build changes the cache namespace. The current workflow is
 local and exposes no distributed worker protocol.
 
diff --git a/docs/user-manual.md b/docs/user-manual.md
index c68c877..92b2c4e 100644
--- a/docs/user-manual.md
+++ b/docs/user-manual.md
@@ -737,7 +737,7 @@ Malformed batches are rejected as a whole:
 
 ```python
 for bad in ([{"id": "a", "parameters": [1, 0]}, {"id": "a", "parameters": [0, 1]}],
-            [{"id": "x", "parameters": [1, 0], "colour": "red"}]):
+            [{"id": "x", "parameters": [1, 0], "color": "red"}]):
     try:
         prepared.batch(bad)
     except ValueError as error:
@@ -754,7 +754,7 @@ except ValueError as error:
 
 ```text
 ValueError: invalid or duplicate candidate id, or parameter vector exceeds limit
-ValueError: unknown field `colour`, expected one of `id`, `parameters`, `trace` at line 1 column 10
+ValueError: unknown field `color`, expected one of `id`, `parameters`, `trace` at line 1 column 9
 ValueError: invalid budget or batch size
 ValueError: ragged parameter rows
 ```
@@ -935,8 +935,8 @@ long closure fifo complete 79.0
 Each returned row has `scenario`, `key`, `build_sha256`, `model_sha256` and the full
 `record`. The cache key hashes the native extension file, the scenario ID, the model, the
 candidate and the budget without `cancel_file`. Complete, invalid and infeasible results
-are cached; cancelled and time-limited attempts stay in the `attempts` journal and are
-retried. A different wheel build uses a new cache namespace. The command-line driver
+are cached; records with any other status (`work_limit`, `wall_limit` or `cancelled`)
+stay only in the `attempts` journal and are evaluated again by the next run. A different wheel build uses a new cache namespace. The command-line driver
 `validation/run_campaign.py MODULE MANIFEST DATABASE` runs a manifest such as
 `models/campaign.json` with four workers.
 
